## Skills

Vendor-authored (MathWorks, BSD-3-Clause) procedures for MATLAB/Simulink work. **Check these before
improvising a MATLAB/Simulink approach** — if one covers the task, follow it rather than inventing a
method.

`.claude/skills/` (auto-discovered) holds the vendor catalog plus a handful of local extras:

- **Vendor symlinks** into `~/.matlab/agentic-toolkits/` — the official MATLAB + Simulink Agentic
  Toolkit catalog, installed and managed by `setupAgenticToolkit`. Update them with
  `setupAgenticToolkit("update")`; never edit them in place.
- **Local extras** — real folders/files for anything project-specific not present in the vendor
  catalog (custom cheat-sheets, custom Model Advisor checks, project conventions).

**How to use one:** read its `SKILL.md` first. Only open `references/` or `scripts/` when `SKILL.md`
says to — those are large and meant to load on demand.

**Trigger table** — fill in with whatever's relevant to your project; browse `.claude/skills/` for
anything not listed here:

| Trigger in the request | Skill |
|---|---|
| "is the model compliant", MISRA / JMAAB / ISO 26262 / DO-178C, Model Advisor run | `checking-model-compliance` |
| "write a custom check", edit-time check, auto-fix check | `check-authoring` |
| Build or edit a Simulink model programmatically | `building-simulink-models` |
| Run/configure a simulation | `simulating-simulink-models` |
| Write or run model tests | `testing-simulink-models`, `authoring-simulink-inputs` |
| Fault injection, safety analysis | `inject-faults`, `manage-safety-analysis` |
| "draft requirements from the model" | `generate-requirement-drafts` |
| "write a spec / test plan / implementation plan" for an algorithm | `specifying-mbd-algorithms` |
| System Composer, architecture layers, stereotypes, allocations | `building-architecture-models` |
| Project paths broken, model refs, labels, add files to project | `managing-simulink-projects` |
| Register/curate custom block libraries; restrict usable blocks | `setup-custom-libraries`, `configuring-block-policy` |
| "wrong value at t=X", "block outputs the wrong thing", step through sim | `simulink-debug-commandline` |
| "simulation is slow", compare two runs | `simulink-profiler-analyzer` |
| "model takes forever to load/compile" | `simulink-profile-initialization` |
| Solver errors, step size, zero-crossings, algebraic loops | `simulink-solver-profiler-analyzer` |
| "file a bug", "document this defect" | `filing-bug-reports` |

### Which skills can actually run here

Verified on <date>. Only <list your licensed toolboxes> are installed (license: <type>).

| Skill | Status | Blocker |
|---|---|---|
| `building-simulink-models`, `simulating-simulink-models`, the profiler/debugger skills | Usable | — |
| `specifying-mbd-algorithms`, `filing-bug-reports` | Usable | Templates only, no toolbox needed |
| `generate-requirement-drafts` | Degraded | No Requirements Toolbox → use its YAML fallback |
| `testing-simulink-models` | Degraded | No Simulink Test → no `sltest.TestCase`; use plain `sim` + `assert` |
| `checking-model-compliance`, `check-authoring` | **Blocked** | No Simulink Check → no Model Advisor |
| `building-architecture-models` | **Blocked** | No System Composer, no Requirements Toolbox |

When a skill is blocked, say so and stop — do not fake Model Advisor output or invent compliance
results. `detect_matlab_toolboxes` settles any doubt in one call.

## MATLAB MCP

Configured in `.mcp.json` as server name `matlab` (project scope, stdio).
**Restart Claude Code after editing it** — MCP servers load at session start.

Prefer the `model_*` tools over hand-written `set_param`/`get_param` — they are what the skills
assume. Cold start is ≈20–30 s for the first call; later calls in the same session are fast.

Facts worth not rediscovering:

- Binary used is the toolkit's `~/.matlab/agentic-toolkits/bin/matlab-mcp-server.exe`.
- `startup.m` in the server's working folder runs `satk_initialize()` + `addpath(genpath(...))`
  automatically. **Without `satk_initialize()` every `model_*` tool fails.**
- `--log-folder=<short path>` is deliberate, not cosmetic — the server opens a unix-domain socket
  inside its log folder; long paths fail with `socket path is too long`. Keep it short and writable.
- `--matlab-session-mode=auto` is deliberate too — `existing` only works when a MATLAB with
  `satk_initialize` is *already* running; `auto` falls back to starting one.
  **Re-running `setupAgenticToolkit("configure")` will overwrite `.mcp.json`** — re-apply these
  settings afterward.
